.\" git-tree(1) — manual page
.TH "GIT-TREE" "1" "July 2026" "git-tree v1.1.0" "Git Manual"

.SH NAME
git-tree \- Display Git-tracked files in a tree structure with syntax highlighting

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit tree\fR [\fIdirectory\fR] [\fB\-a\fR] [\fB\-A\fR] [\fB\-d\fR] [\fB\-L\fR \fIN\fR] [\fB\-\-color=\fIWHEN\fR] [\fB\-\-git-status\fR] [\fB\-\-no-git-status\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBgit-tree\fR renders the repository's tracked file hierarchy as an
ASCII tree, similar to the system \fBtree\fR(1) utility but scoped to
files known to Git.
.PP
By default only \fBtracked\fR files are shown (\fBgit ls-files --cached\fR),
and each entry is prefixed with a one-character \fBGit status\fR indicator
(committed / modified / staged) following \fBeza --git\fR.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-all\fR
Include untracked files (excluding \fB.gitignore\fR'd).
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-all\-files\fR
Include ALL files, including \fB.gitignore\fR'd ones.
.TP
\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-dirs\-only\fR
Show directories only; omit regular files.
.TP
\fB\-L\fR \fIN\fR
Limit the display depth to \fIN\fR levels (like \fBtree -L\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-color=\fIWHEN\fR
When to colorize output: \fBalways\fR, \fBnever\fR, or \fBauto\fR (default).
.TP
\fB\-\-git-status\fR
Show Git status prefixes (default). Provided for explicitness.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-git\-status\fR
Suppress Git status prefixes and restore the original layout.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR
Show brief help and exit.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Show this manual page.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show version information and exit.

.SH GIT STATUS PREFIXES
Each entry is prefixed with a one-character Git state indicator:
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
_
State|Prefix|Default color
_
committed| (blank)|type color
modified|M|Yellow bold
staged|+|Green bold
untracked|?|Red bold
_
.TE
.PP
Directories show the aggregate state of their descendants
(staged > modified > untracked). A file both staged and modified is
reported as staged. Regular-file names are recolored by state; directories,
executables and symlinks keep their type color.

.SH COLOR RULES
Colors follow \fBLS_COLORS\fR conventions:
.TS
tab(|);
l l l.
_
Entry|LS_COLORS key|Default
_
Directory|di|Bold blue
Executable|ex|Bold green
Symlink|ln|Bold cyan
Orphaned link|or|Red background
Hidden file|—|Dim
Tree connector|—|Dim
Git: modified|gm|Yellow bold
Git: staged|ga|Green bold
Git: untracked|gu|Red bold
_
.TE
.PP
Set \fBNO_COLOR=1\fR to disable all color output.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Show entire repository (tracked files only)
$ \fBgit tree\fR

# Limit depth to 2 levels
$ \fBgit tree -L 2\fR

# Show only directories
$ \fBgit tree -d\fR

# Include untracked files
$ \fBgit tree -a\fR

# Force color output even when piped
$ \fBgit tree --color=always | less -R\fR
.fi

.SH "SEE ALSO"
